# ============================================================================
# Meridian Estates — what is deliberately not in version control.
#
# Every entry here is either reproducible from the checked-in sources or a
# secret. The repository is public, so the distinction matters: build output is
# merely noise, but an ignored secret is one that can be rotated.
# ============================================================================

# --- Dependencies and build output: reproducible, never committed ------------
node_modules/
target/
dist/

# --- Local runtime state -----------------------------------------------------
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Logs and editor scratch -------------------------------------------------
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# `backend/.env` holds this installation's local database password and token
# signing key. The committed template is `backend/.env.example`, which carries
# placeholders only. A host environment variable always wins over `.env`, so a
# deployment never needs this file.
#
# These two rules come after the pattern above them on purpose: a later negation
# re-includes a file an earlier rule excluded, which is the only way to keep the
# `.env.example` templates visible while ignoring everything else that is one.
.env
.env.local
*.env.local

!.env.example
!*.env.example
